---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { icons } from "../../components/icons";

const articleSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Article",
  headline: "Into the knockouts at IFAC 2026",
  description:
    "15th of 55 international teams and our first two head-to-head knockout wins — four days in Busan at the 29th RoboRacer competition, on a rebuilt car.",
  image: new URL("/assets/pit-notes/ifac-2026/banner.jpg", Astro.site).toString(),
  datePublished: "2026-09-11",
  author: { "@type": "Organization", name: "NTU DeepSpeed", url: Astro.site?.toString() },
  publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "NTU DeepSpeed", url: Astro.site?.toString() },
  mainEntityOfPage: new URL(Astro.url.pathname, Astro.site).toString(),
};
---

<Base
  active="pit-notes"
  title="Into the knockouts at IFAC 2026"
  description="15th of 55 international teams and our first two head-to-head knockout wins — four days in Busan at the 29th RoboRacer competition, on a rebuilt car."
  ogType="article"
  ogImage="/assets/pit-notes/ifac-2026/banner.jpg"
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <meta property="article:published_time" content="2026-09-11" />
    <script is:inline type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(articleSchema)} />
  </Fragment>
  <article class="article-wrap">
    <a href="/pit-notes/" class="article-back">
      <Fragment set:html={icons.arrowLeft()} />
      All pit notes
    </a>
    <div class="hero-eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:12px;color:var(--accent)" data-reveal>
      Race report · Sep 11 · 2026
    </div>
    <h1 style="font-size:clamp(40px,6vw,64px);margin-bottom:16px" data-reveal>
      Into the knockouts at IFAC 2026
    </h1>
    <p class="hero-sub" style="margin-bottom:24px" data-reveal>
      Our second race of the year: four days in Busan at the 29th RoboRacer Autonomous Racing
      Competition, on a rebuilt platform and with a lot more confidence.
    </p>
    <div class="article-byline" data-reveal>
      <span>By the Busan crew</span>
      <span>·</span>
      <span>4 min read</span>
    </div>
    <figure class="article-figure wide">
      <img
        class="article-media"
        data-reveal
        src="/assets/pit-notes/ifac-2026/banner.jpg"
        alt="IFAC Busan, South Korea — the NTU DeepSpeed crew with their cars, over a three-stage run: 01 pre-race, 02 practice day, 03 head to head"
      />
      <figcaption>IFAC 2026 · Busan, South Korea</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <div class="article-body">
      <p>
        We're back from Busan after racing at the 29th RoboRacer Competition, IFAC 2026. 🇰🇷 This
        was our second race of the year — after ICRA in Vienna back in June, we brought a rebuilt
        platform and a lot more confidence to Korea.
      </p>
      <div class="tele" style="margin-bottom:32px" data-reveal>
        <div class="hero-eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:16px">IFAC 2026 · results</div>
        <div class="tele-row"><span class="k">Head-to-head</span><span class="v red">BO32 Finals</span></div>
        <div class="tele-row"><span class="k">Knockout races won</span><span class="v">2</span></div>
        <div class="tele-row"><span class="k">Overall</span><span class="v red">15th / 55</span></div>
      </div>
      <p>
        We advanced to the BO32 Head-to-Head Finals, winning our first two knockout races as a
        team, and finished 15th overall out of 55 international teams.
      </p>
      <figure class="article-figure">
        <img
          class="article-media"
          data-reveal
          src="/assets/pit-notes/ifac-2026/head-to-head.jpg"
          alt="The white-bodied DeepSpeed car alongside SNU ZERO's black-bodied car during a head-to-head race"
        />
        <figcaption>Racing SNU ZERO in the knockouts</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="article-figure">
        <img
          class="article-media"
          data-reveal
          src="/assets/pit-notes/ifac-2026/celebration.jpg"
          alt="A DeepSpeed team member celebrating with both fists raised as the race is called"
        />
        <figcaption>Winning a knockout race</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <h2>A rebuilt car</h2>
      <p>
        One of the biggest changes since ICRA: we upgraded our hardware. Onboard compute went from
        our original NVIDIA Jetson to an Intel NUC, alongside a full swap of our servos and motor.
        That gave us a more reliable, more capable platform to actually push in Busan.
      </p>
      <figure class="article-figure">
        <img
          class="article-media"
          data-reveal
          src="/assets/pit-notes/ifac-2026/car-detail.jpg"
          alt="Top-down view of the rebuilt car showing the Intel NUC, servos and wiring under the body shell"
        />
        <figcaption>The rebuilt platform: new compute, new servos, new motor</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <p>
        On the software side, the biggest shift was building our own Waypoint Studio. What used to
        be countless hours of manual trajectory generation at ICRA became a workflow where we could
        iterate cleanly and apply tweaks straight from what we saw in practice sessions.
      </p>
      <figure class="article-figure">
        <img
          class="article-media"
          data-reveal
          src="/assets/pit-notes/ifac-2026/pit-laptops.jpg"
          alt="Two team members working on laptops trackside between runs"
        />
        <figcaption>Iterating between practice sessions</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <h2>Not everything goes to plan</h2>
      <p>
        On day one we found out the tires we'd flown in from Singapore had no grip on the venue's
        concrete floor. UNICORN Racing offered to help and got us a set that worked perfectly.
        We're genuinely grateful for that.
      </p>
      <figure class="article-figure">
        <img
          class="article-media"
          data-reveal
          src="/assets/pit-notes/ifac-2026/car-on-track.jpg"
          alt="The DeepSpeed car running on the bare concrete floor of the Busan venue"
        />
        <figcaption>The venue's concrete — the surface our tires had no answer for</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <h2>How far the field has come</h2>
      <p>
        Beyond the results, this week was a reminder of just how far the field has come. We were
        genuinely surprised by how many teams could avoid obstacles cleanly at speeds much higher
        than we expected. Watching that, taking notes in the pits, and getting pushed to be better
        by teams from around the world is exactly what makes RoboRacer special. 🔥
      </p>
      <figure class="article-figure">
        <img
          class="article-media"
          data-reveal
          src="/assets/pit-notes/ifac-2026/arena.jpg"
          alt="The Busan competition hall: the barrier-lined track in front of the RoboRacer stage"
        />
        <figcaption>The hall at BEXCO, Busan</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <h2>Thank you</h2>
      <figure class="article-figure">
        <img
          class="article-media"
          data-reveal
          src="/assets/pit-notes/ifac-2026/team-with-cars.jpg"
          alt="Five NTU DeepSpeed members with their car in front of the IFAC 2026 RoboRacer backdrop"
        />
        <figcaption>The Busan crew, car in hand</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <p>
        Huge thanks to the team: Ting-Ju Chen, Yun-Tung Lee, Nathan Lee, Abhiram Chennupati,
        Sarvajana Hari, Kah Lok Wong, and Baba Moolya. We would not have been able to achieve this
        without you.
      </p>
      <p>
        A special thanks to the NTU College of Computing and Data Science for providing the testing
        venue and resources that made this run possible.
      </p>
      <p>
        Finally, thank you to the RoboRacer Foundation and the IFAC 2026 organizers for running
        such a smooth, well-organized event for 55 teams from start to finish — and to the teams we
        competed against, for making it a genuinely welcoming community off the track.
      </p>
      <p>See you at the next starting line. 🏁🏎</p>
    </div>
    <div class="checkered" style="padding:24px 0">🏁</div>
    <a class="btn ghost" href="/pit-notes/" style="text-decoration:none">All pit notes</a>
  </article>
</Base>

<script>
  import "../../scripts/reading-progress";
</script>
